msgid "La carte montre les propriétaires et les fortifications publiques. Les forces et les stocks rivaux restent secrets ; vos rapports gardent les observations du jour où ils ont été écrits. Le devis annonce départ, combat et retour prévu. Les tentatives de siège suivent actuellement ce même calendrier."
msgstr "The map shows owners and public fortifications. Rival forces and stocks remain secret; your reports preserve observations from their writing date. The preview gives departure, combat and expected return dates. Siege attempts currently follow this same schedule."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "La préparation du matériel de siège a commencé."
msgstr "Preparation of siege equipment has begun."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Le raid sur nos villages a coûté la vie à {p0} de nos Fidèles. Les assaillants ont emporté {p1} Mesures et en ont détruit {p2} autres. Ces pertes diminuent la récolte en préparation ; la production continue. "
msgstr "The foray on our villages cost {p0} of our Fidèles their lives. The attackers carried off {p1} Measures and destroyed another {p2}. These losses reduce the pending harvest; production continues. "

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Le rendement par habitant présent progresse de 100 à 115, 130 puis 200 Mesures par lune. Les revenus restent indisponibles jusqu’au versement annuel."
msgstr "Yield per present resident rises from 100 to 115, 130 and then 200 Measures per Moon. Income remains unavailable until annual payment."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Les assaillants de cette cité ignorent 25 % du bonus des fortifications."
msgstr "Attackers from this city ignore 25% of the fortification bonus."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Les assaillants de cette cité ignorent 50 % du bonus des fortifications."
msgstr "Attackers from this city ignore 50% of the fortification bonus."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Les ateliers de transport ont commencé leur ouvrage."
msgstr "The transport workshops have begun their work."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Les bonus militaires remplacent les niveaux précédents. Chaque contingent garde son équipement, son transport et son matériel de siège de départ. Le transport augmente le butin emportable, sans améliorer les chances de victoire."
msgstr "Military bonuses replace previous levels. Each contingent retains its departure equipment, transport and siege gear. Transport increases carrying capacity without improving the chances of victory."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Les travaux de surveillance ont commencé."
msgstr "Work on surveillance has begun."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Les travaux des réserves protégées ont commencé."
msgstr "Work on protected reserves has begun."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Mettre une partie de la récolte à l’abri."
msgstr "Shelter part of the harvest."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Mobiliser davantage de défenseurs contre les raids."
msgstr "Mobilize more defenders against forays."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Murailles"
msgstr "City walls"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Ordres en attente"
msgstr "Pending orders"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Organiser la surveillance"
msgstr "Organize surveillance"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Palais renforcé"
msgstr "Reinforced palace"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Palissades de bois"
msgstr "Wooden palisades"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Petit arsenal"
msgstr "Small arsenal"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Piller"
msgstr "Plunder"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Postes de veille"
msgstr "Watch posts"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Pour une première partie, choisissez le calendrier manuel. Vous pourrez lire chaque nouvelle avant de passer à la lune suivante."
msgstr "For your first game, choose the manual calendar. You can read each report before advancing to the next Moon."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Protéger les récoltes"
msgstr "Protect the harvest"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Préparer le matériel de siège"
msgstr "Prepare siege equipment"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Rapporter davantage de butin."
msgstr "Bring back more loot."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Restaurer {work}"
msgstr "Restore {work}"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Rigoles et petites digues"
msgstr "Channels and small dikes"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Récolte protégée du pillage et des destructions : 400 000 Mesures."
msgstr "Harvest protected from theft and destruction: 400,000 Measures."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Récolte protégée du pillage et des destructions : 800 000 Mesures."
msgstr "Harvest protected from theft and destruction: 800,000 Measures."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Récoltes et pillages"
msgstr "Harvests and forays"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Réduire l’avantage des fortifications adverses."
msgstr "Reduce the advantage of enemy fortifications."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Réserves souterraines"
msgstr "Underground reserves"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Réserves villageoises"
msgstr "Village reserves"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Sans fortifications"
msgstr "No fortifications"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Sans matériel de siège"
msgstr "No siege equipment"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Sans surveillance, 20 %, 30 % ou 40 % des Fidèles disponibles défendent les villages. Les postes de veille garantissent 40 %, les tours 60 %. Les fortifications protègent seulement des captures. Le matériel de siège réduit leur bonus, jamais la défense de base."
msgstr "Without surveillance, 20%, 30% or 40% of available Fidèles defend the villages. Watch posts guarantee 40%, towers 60%. Fortifications protect only against capture. Siege equipment reduces their bonus, never base defense."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Tours de guet"
msgstr "Watchtowers"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Train de transport"
msgstr "Transport train"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Transport ordinaire"
msgstr "Ordinary transport"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Un raid vise la récolte en préparation, jamais le grenier. Après protection de 200 000, 400 000 ou 800 000 Mesures, un quart du reste est exposé. Une victoire permet d’en emporter 60 %, dans la limite du transport, et en détruit 20 %. Ces pertes réduisent le versement annuel, sans interrompre la production ni les chantiers."
msgstr "A foray targets the pending harvest, never the granary. After protecting 200,000, 400,000 or 800,000 Measures, a quarter of the remainder is exposed. Victory can carry away 60% of that portion, within transport capacity, and destroys 20%. These losses reduce annual payment without interrupting production or works."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Valider l’action"
msgstr "Validate action"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Veille ordinaire"
msgstr "Ordinary watch"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "ont achevé {work}"
msgstr "have completed {work}"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "ont restauré {work}"
msgstr "have restored {work}"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "« Valider l’action » vous mène à la relecture, sans rien réserver. Vérifiez les termes ; « Confirmer et sceller l’ordre » engage ensuite les fonds et les équipes ou les hommes annoncés. Les bénéfices d’un ouvrage viennent à son achèvement."
msgstr "“Validate action” opens the review without reserving anything. Check the terms; “Confirm and seal the order” then commits the stated funds and teams or troops. A work’s benefits begin on completion."

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Échelles d’assaut"
msgstr "Assault ladders"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Équipement des ateliers d’armement"
msgstr "Weapons workshop equipment"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Équipement du grand arsenal"
msgstr "Great arsenal equipment"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Équipement du petit arsenal"
msgstr "Small arsenal equipment"

#. Approved playability revision, October 2026.
msgid "Villages dispersés : un nouveau pillage pourra arriver à partir de la lune %(moon)s. La capture reste possible."
msgstr "Dispersed villages: a new foray may arrive from Moon %(moon)s. Capture remains possible."

msgid "Bonus défensif local restauré : +{before} % → +{after} %."
msgstr "Restored local defense bonus: +{before}% to +{after}%."

msgid "L’attaque a réussi ; la défense a cédé."
msgstr "The attack succeeded; the defense gave way."

msgid "L’attaque a échoué ; la défense a tenu."
msgstr "The attack failed; the defense held."

msgid "Le livre du règne"
msgstr "The book of the reign"

msgid "Le règne est achevé. Voici les lettres conservées, dans l’ordre des lunes, et les comptes enregistrés à leur clôture."
msgstr "The reign is over. Here are the preserved letters in Moon order, and the accounts recorded at each closure."

msgid "Les maisons du livre"
msgstr "Houses in the book"

msgid "Toutes les maisons"
msgstr "All houses"

msgid "Télécharger le livre pour analyse (JSON)"
msgstr "Download the book for analysis (JSON)"

msgid "Les lettres d’un même événement peuvent figurer pour plusieurs destinataires : ce sont leurs témoignages, pas des événements supplémentaires. Les comptes décrivent la fin de chaque lune enregistrée."
msgstr "Letters about one event may appear for several recipients: they are their accounts, not additional events. The accounts describe the end of each recorded Moon."

msgid "Certains comptes mensuels n’ont pas été conservés. Les lettres disponibles et les comptes finaux restent accessibles ; les mois manquants sont signalés dans le téléchargement, sans reconstitution."
msgstr "Some monthly accounts were not preserved. Available letters and final accounts remain accessible; missing Moons are listed in the download, without reconstruction."

msgid "Les comptes conservés"
msgstr "Preserved accounts"

msgid "Les comptes finaux"
msgstr "Final accounts"

msgid "Habitants : %(population)s. Mesures en réserve : %(stock)s. Prélèvement accumulé : %(tax)s."
msgstr "Inhabitants: %(population)s. Stored Measures: %(stock)s. Accrued levy: %(tax)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid " Les assaillants portaient le sceau de {house}. "
msgstr " The attackers bore the seal of {house}. "

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid " Nos hommes ont incendié une partie des récoltes accessibles."
msgstr " Our men burned part of the accessible crops."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid " Nos survivants sont au nombre de {count}. "
msgstr " Our survivors number {count}. "

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid " Survivants : {survivors}. Coût payé : {cost} Mesures. "
msgstr " Survivors: {survivors}. Paid cost: {cost} Measures. "

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid " Un ouvrage a été endommagé : {work}."
msgstr " A structure was damaged: {work}."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid " Un ouvrage a été endommagé : {work}. Il fonctionne au niveau inférieur jusqu’à sa réparation."
msgstr " A structure was damaged: {work}. It operates one level lower until repaired."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid " Victimes parmi les habitants non engagés : {count}. "
msgstr " Casualties among residents outside the fighting: {count}. "

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "%(origin)s → %(target)s : %(cargo)s Mesures. Arrivée prévue à la lune %(moon)s."
msgstr "%(origin)s to %(target)s: %(cargo)s Measures. Arrival expected at Moon %(moon)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Acheminer des ressources"
msgstr "Send resources"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Achèvement : lune %(finish)s. Premier effet : lune %(effect)s. Réserves après paiement : %(remaining)s Mesures."
msgstr "Completion: Moon %(finish)s. First effect: Moon %(effect)s. Reserves after payment: %(remaining)s Measures."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Après départ : %(remaining)s Mesures libres ; besoin d’un mois de siège : %(need)s."
msgstr "After departure: %(remaining)s free Measures; one month's siege needs: %(need)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Après paiement et départ des hommes : %(remaining)s Mesures libres ; besoin d’un mois de siège : %(need)s."
msgstr "After payment and the men's departure: %(remaining)s free Measures; one month's siege needs: %(need)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Attention : il manque %(missing)s Mesures pour tenir un mois de siège après cet ordre."
msgstr "Warning: %(missing)s Measures short of one month's siege supplies after this order."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Attention : il manque %(missing)s Mesures pour tenir un mois de siège après les réservations."
msgstr "Warning: %(missing)s Measures short of one month's siege supplies after reservations."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Attention : moins d’un mois de réserves de siège après ce chantier."
msgstr "Warning: less than one month's siege supplies after this work."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Attention : moins d’un mois de réserves de siège après ce départ."
msgstr "Warning: less than one month's siege supplies after this departure."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Aucun témoignage de combat conservé pour cette cible. Ses effectifs, ses réserves et ses ouvrages non observés restent inconnus."
msgstr "No battle testimony has been kept for this target. Its forces, reserves and unobserved structures remain unknown."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Besoin d’un mois de siège : %(need)s Mesures déjà engrangées."
msgstr "One month's siege needs: %(need)s Measures already in store."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cargaison conservée à {city} : {kept} Mesures ; cargaison perdue ou sans place : {lost}. Frais payés : {fee} Mesures."
msgstr "Cargo retained at {city}: {kept} Measures; cargo lost or without room: {lost}. Fees paid: {fee} Measures."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cargaison en Mesures"
msgstr "Cargo in Measures"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Ce chantier s’achèverait après la fin du règne."
msgstr "This work would finish after the end of the reign."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Ce que nous savons de cette cible"
msgstr "What we know about this target"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Ces moyens sont figés au départ. La défense réelle, les renforts et les réserves ennemies restent inconnus ; une observation datée décrit un ancien combat, jamais une garantie pour le prochain."
msgstr "These means are fixed at departure. Actual defenses, reinforcements and enemy reserves remain unknown; a dated observation describes a past battle, never a guarantee for the next one."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cet ouvrage ne nécessite aucune réparation."
msgstr "This structure needs no repair."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cette alerte mesure une capacité de ravitaillement, pas une attaque annoncée. Les secours automatiques dépendent des cités encore amicales et disponibles ; ils ne sont pas garantis."
msgstr "This warning measures supply capacity, not an announced attack. Automatic relief depends on cities still being friendly and available; it is not guaranteed."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cette projection conserve les habitants présents et le rendement actuels jusqu’à la récolte. Elle exclut les futurs mouvements, pertes, pillages et changements de rendement, y compris les chantiers en cours. Ce repère n’est ni un revenu garanti ni de l’argent déjà dépensable."
msgstr "This projection holds the current population present and yield constant until the harvest. It excludes future movements, losses, forays and changes in yield, including ongoing works. This estimate is neither guaranteed income nor money already available to spend."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Chaque cité finance ses travaux. Pour une expédition, chaque origine paie ses hommes et une part des frais fixes proportionnelle à son effectif."
msgstr "Each city funds its works. For an expedition, each origin pays for its men and a share of the fixed fee proportional to its contingent."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Chaque cité finance son ouvrage ou sa contribution. Aucun autre grenier ne comble son manque."
msgstr "Each city funds its work or contribution. No other granary covers its shortfall."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Choisir une cité"
msgstr "Choose a city"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Choisissez deux cités distinctes de votre maison."
msgstr "Choose two distinct cities belonging to your house."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cité de départ"
msgstr "Origin city"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cité de frontière : accessible à une maison ennemie."
msgstr "Frontier city: accessible to an enemy house."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cité intérieure : pas de frontière ennemie directe."
msgstr "Interior city: no direct enemy frontier."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Cité à ravitailler"
msgstr "City to supply"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Comparer les contingents"
msgstr "Compare contingents"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Comprendre le butin"
msgstr "Understand the spoils"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Comprendre les convois"
msgstr "Understand convoys"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Convoi déjà engagé"
msgstr "Convoy already committed"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "De %(origin)s vers %(target)s : %(cargo)s Mesures de cargaison et %(fee)s Mesures de frais. Départ à la lune %(departure)s, arrivée à la lune %(arrival)s, après les combats."
msgstr "From %(origin)s to %(target)s: %(cargo)s Measures of cargo and %(fee)s Measures in fees. Departure at Moon %(departure)s, arrival at Moon %(arrival)s, after the battles."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Défenses de la cité"
msgstr "City defenses"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Départ : lune %(departure)s · Combat : lune %(combat)s · Retour : lune %(arrival)s."
msgstr "Departure: Moon %(departure)s · Battle: Moon %(combat)s · Return: Moon %(arrival)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Départ à la clôture de la lune %(departure)s ; arrivée à la clôture de la lune %(arrival)s, après les combats."
msgstr "Departure at the close of Moon %(departure)s; arrival at the close of Moon %(arrival)s, after the battles."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Examiner les travaux possibles"
msgstr "Examine available works"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Il faudra conserver au moins %(amount)s Mesures de butin pour rembourser cette expédition."
msgstr "At least %(amount)s Measures of spoils must be retained to repay this expedition."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Il faut réparer cet ouvrage avant de l’améliorer."
msgstr "This structure must be repaired before it can be improved."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Ils rejoignent les Fidèles de votre maison."
msgstr "They rejoin your house's Faithful."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Ils sont démobilisés parmi les habitants, sans rejoindre les Fidèles du nouveau souverain."
msgstr "They are demobilized among the inhabitants, without joining the new sovereign's Faithful."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "La capacité du grenier limite la réception. Si la destination est perdue, le convoi tente de rentrer à l’origine ou au refuge choisi au départ, avec une lune supplémentaire. Sans destination encore amicale à l’arrivée, la cargaison est perdue. Les convois n’ont ni escorte ni interception."
msgstr "Granary capacity limits how much can be received. If the destination is lost, the convoy tries to return to its origin or the refuge chosen at departure, taking one extra Moon. Without a still-friendly destination on arrival, the cargo is lost. Convoys have no escort or interception."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "La cargaison doit contenir de 1 à 500 000 Mesures entières."
msgstr "Cargo must contain between 1 and 500,000 whole Measures."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "La destination a changé de maître. Le convoi tentera de rejoindre {city} à la lune {moon}."
msgstr "The destination has changed ruler. The convoy will try to reach {city} at Moon {moon}."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "La garnison locale sera mieux protégée contre les captures ; les réserves restent nécessaires pour tenir un siège."
msgstr "The local garrison will be better protected against capture; reserves are still needed to withstand a siege."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le chemin du convoi n’est plus amical."
msgstr "The convoy's route is no longer friendly."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le compte du convoi"
msgstr "The convoy account"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le contingent cherche refuge"
msgstr "The contingent seeks refuge"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le convoi de ressources est parti."
msgstr "The supply convoy has departed."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le convoi exige un chemin entièrement amical."
msgstr "The convoy needs an entirely friendly route."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le convoi fait demi-tour"
msgstr "The convoy turns back"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le convoi fait demi-tour."
msgstr "The convoy turns back."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le délai du règne ou un dommage empêche ce chantier."
msgstr "The end of the reign or damage prevents this work."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le premier effet économique arriverait après la fin du règne."
msgstr "The first economic effect would arrive after the end of the reign."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le prélèvement en préparation ne nourrit pas le siège. Les murs facilitent la défense contre l’assaut, mais ne remplacent pas les réserves. Un chantier ou une expédition peut créer un manque : gardez une marge ou préparez un convoi."
msgstr "The accrued levy cannot feed a siege. Walls help defend against an assault, but cannot replace reserves. Works or expeditions may cause a shortfall: keep a margin or prepare a convoy."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Le seuil de remboursement couvre les frais payés. Il ne compense ni les morts, ni la production perdue pendant l’absence, ni le butin perdu faute de place au retour. La capacité de transport est un plafond, pas une promesse de gain."
msgstr "The repayment threshold covers the fees paid. It does not compensate for deaths, production lost during the absence, or spoils lost for lack of room on return. Carrying capacity is a ceiling, not a promise of profit."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Les rangs adverses ont subi de très lourdes pertes."
msgstr "The enemy ranks suffered very heavy losses."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Les rangs adverses ont subi des pertes sensibles."
msgstr "The enemy ranks suffered noticeable losses."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Les rangs adverses ont été durement éprouvés."
msgstr "The enemy ranks were badly depleted."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Les réparations des ouvrages extérieurs ont commencé."
msgstr "Repairs to the exterior structures have begun."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Les secours de {city}"
msgstr "Relief from {city}"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Lire cette prévision"
msgstr "Read this forecast"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Lune %(moon)s"
msgstr "Moon %(moon)s"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "L’arsenal équipe les Fidèles de son origine en attaque comme en défense. Le matériel de siège réduit l’avantage des murs lors d’une capture ; il ne sert pas au pillage. Le transport augmente le butin que les survivants peuvent rapporter."
msgstr "The arsenal equips its city's Faithful in attack and defense. Siege equipment reduces the walls' advantage during a capture; it has no use in forays. Transport increases the spoils survivors can bring home."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "L’ouvrage retrouvera toute son efficacité ; l’équipe sera occupée pendant la réparation."
msgstr "The structure will regain its full effectiveness; the crew will be occupied during repairs."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "L’ouvrage retrouvera toute son efficacité, sans gagner de niveau."
msgstr "The structure will regain its full effectiveness, without gaining a level."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Moins d’un mois de siège : besoin de %(need)s Mesures ; manque de %(missing)s après les réservations."
msgstr "Less than one month's siege supplies: %(need)s Measures needed; %(missing)s short after reservations."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Niveau bâti : %(built)s · Niveau en service : %(effective)s."
msgstr "Built level: %(built)s · Effective level: %(effective)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Nos convois en route"
msgstr "Our convoys on the road"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Nos témoins ne peuvent apprécier les pertes adverses."
msgstr "Our witnesses cannot judge the enemy's losses."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Nos témoins n’ont constaté aucune perte dans les rangs adverses."
msgstr "Our witnesses saw no losses in the enemy ranks."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Observation de la lune %(moon)s"
msgstr "Observation from Moon %(moon)s"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Ouvrage endommagé"
msgstr "Damaged structure"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Pillage remporté de haute lutte"
msgstr "Hard-fought foray victory"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Pillage sans opposition"
msgstr "Unopposed foray"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Prochaine équipe libérée : lune %(moon)s."
msgstr "Next crew available: Moon %(moon)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Prélèvement estimé à la prochaine récolte : %(amount)s Mesures ; débordement possible : %(overflow)s."
msgstr "Estimated levy at the next harvest: %(amount)s Measures; possible overflow: %(overflow)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Quelques combattants adverses sont tombés."
msgstr "A few enemy fighters fell."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Raid interrompu"
msgstr "Foray abandoned"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Restaurer l’efficacité de cet ouvrage endommagé."
msgstr "Restore the effectiveness of this damaged structure."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Retour du contingent de {city}"
msgstr "Return of the contingent from {city}"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Réparer la surveillance"
msgstr "Repair surveillance"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Réparer les réserves protégées"
msgstr "Repair protected reserves"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Réparer occupe la même équipe que construire. Le niveau bâti est conservé ; le dommage réduit son effet d’un niveau jusqu’à la réparation."
msgstr "Repairs use the same crew as construction. The built level is retained; damage reduces its effect by one level until repaired."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Seuil de protection : {amount} Mesures, plafonné à 90 % de la récolte accumulée."
msgstr "Protection threshold: {amount} Measures, capped at 90 % of the accrued crop."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Tenir un siège"
msgstr "Withstand a siege"

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Transport : jusqu’à %(capacity)s Mesures par survivant."
msgstr "Transport: up to %(capacity)s Measures per survivor."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Travaux en cours ou réservés jusqu’à la lune %(moon)s."
msgstr "Work underway or reserved until Moon %(moon)s."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Un chantier commencé à la lune N et durant trois lunes s’achève à N+3. L’irrigation agit sur le prélèvement à la clôture suivante ; l’argent reste indisponible jusqu’à la récolte. Un ouvrage achevé trop tard peut ne jamais produire son premier effet pendant ce règne."
msgstr "Work started at Moon N and lasting three Moons finishes at N+3. Irrigation affects the levy at the following closure; the money remains unavailable until harvest. A structure completed too late may never produce its first effect during this reign."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Un convoi est déjà engagé depuis cette cité."
msgstr "A convoy is already committed from this city."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Un convoi transporte au plus 500 000 Mesures entre deux cités amicales reliées. La cargaison et les frais sont payés au départ ; seule la cargaison arrive deux lunes plus tard. Les frais sont de 10 %, 7 % ou 5 % selon le transport de l’origine, arrondis au supérieur."
msgstr "A convoy carries at most 500,000 Measures between two connected friendly cities. Cargo and fees are paid at departure; only the cargo arrives two Moons later. Fees are 10 %, 7 % or 5 % depending on the origin's transport, rounded up."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Un raid qui fait perdre des ressources, des habitants ou un ouvrage à sa cible déclenche deux lunes de répit, même après une défaite des assaillants. Une attaque sans perte pour la cible ne déclenche aucun répit. Les dégâts de la lune de récolte sont retirés avant son versement."
msgstr "A foray that costs its target resources, inhabitants or a structure triggers two Moons of respite, even after the attackers' defeat. An attack causing no loss to its target triggers no respite. Damage in the harvest Moon is deducted before payment."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Un raid vise le prélèvement accumulé. Les abris protègent au plus 90 % de cette récolte ; un quart du reste est exposé. Une victoire nette permet d’en emporter 60 %, une victoire disputée 30 %. Le transport des survivants limite toujours le butin. Les destructions restent limitées par les hommes qui survivent ; production et chantiers continuent."
msgstr "A foray targets the accrued levy. Shelters protect at most 90 % of this crop; a quarter of the remainder is exposed. A clear victory allows 60 % to be taken, a hard-fought victory 30 %. Survivors' transport always limits the spoils. Destruction is limited by surviving men; production and works continue."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Un raid vise les prélèvements accumulés avant la récolte annuelle, pas les réserves déjà engrangées. Les abris et les pillages précédents réduisent les prises possibles. Une victoire militaire peut donc rester déficitaire."
msgstr "A foray targets levies accrued before the annual harvest, not reserves already in store. Shelters and earlier forays reduce potential spoils. A military victory may therefore still lose money."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Un siège ponctuel représente un mois. Si l’armée ennemie dépasse la défense de campagne sans pouvoir franchir les murs, chaque habitant présent exige 500 Mesures déjà engrangées. À l’égalité exacte, la cité tient et consomme ce montant ; en dessous, elle consomme ce qui reste et capitule."
msgstr "A single siege attempt represents one month. If the enemy army exceeds the field defense without breaching the walls, each inhabitant present needs 500 Measures already in store. At exact equality, the city holds and consumes that amount; below it, the city consumes what remains and capitulates."

#: Strategic preparation and recipient reports
msgid "Une cité possède une seule équipe. Construire et réparer mobilisent cette même équipe ; un décret scellé la réserve déjà. Aucun autre chantier ne peut commencer ici avant sa libération."
msgstr "A city has one crew. Building and repairing use this same crew; a sealed decree already reserves it. No other work can start here until the crew is released."

